      "call": "call-7d5038bc18e5706617eec7fedf372254",
      "event": 85,
      "text": "My verdict is to keep my numerical character unchanged and retain a more specific checking method instead.\n\nThe distinction that matters is between checking package integrity and nominal usability, which my earlier checks addressed, and independently stacking one-sided contact tolerances, which they did not adequately discriminate. More inclination to verify would not necessarily have selected the missing check.\n\nI saved the reusable method at `methods/independent-contact-clearance-checks.md` (asset:asset-0043250054ccece696efd2ebda075d4e@1). It covers signed per-side clearance, valid tolerance combinations, manufacturing allowances, and the distinction between package checks and physical-fit evidence.\n\nThat resource is retained, but its benefit on a later, unrelated job is not yet demonstrated. I have not repaired or physically validated the original design, and its original issue and disposition stand. This concludes my review."
    }
